5,1,1,talk,Servas,,We must look at the past. I will examine the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts and the record of cross-unit standardization efforts.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,I’m worried about where the money actually comes from. I’ll check the capital budget and software allowance.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Sakura,,I’m curious about the real-world conditions! I’ll look into network coverage at customer plants and in-house developer availability.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,I will examine the time lost to copying existing records and the misrouted deliveries in the incident logs.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Asuka,,I will investigate the staffing of the coordination group and the handling of vendor queries.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Servas,,"@Daisuke, your caution is wise. Knowing the source of funds is the first step to understanding what we can truly afford.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Daisuke,,"Thank you, Servas. It’s just that the budget line is frozen, so I need to be sure before we commit to anything.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Ryuji, do you think those misrouted deliveries are connected to the copying time you’re checking?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, likely. The logs show duplicate addresses causing the errors, which mirrors the time wasted copying inconsistent records.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, that duplication sounds like a symptom of the staffing gap I’m investigating. We need to know who is actually absorbing that daily waste.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, you are right. The human cost is often the most overlooked expense. I will see if the past failures reflect this same strain.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Servas, I hope the past shows us where the money went, so we don’t repeat the same mistakes with this year’s fund.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, I hope the budget isn’t a dead end! I’m checking if our developers are even free to build anything, so we don’t promise the impossible.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, if the developers are unavailable, the technical feasibility of any proposal becomes a theoretical exercise rather than a practical one.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, exactly. If the builders are tied up, the proposal is just a wish. I need to know who absorbs the overflow when the rota breaks.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Servas,,I will now review the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts and the record of cross-unit standardization efforts.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Daisuke,,I’ll review the capital budget and software allowance to see what’s actually available.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Sakura,,I’ll check the network coverage and developer availability to see if the groundwork is actually solid.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will review the time lost to copying records and the misrouted deliveries to quantify the daily operational losses.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Asuka,,I will review the coordination group staffing and vendor query handling to see who is actually doing the work.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
