60,3,1,talk,Servas,,"The candidates are A: Supplier Data Hub, B: Workflow Assistant, C: Training Studio, and D: Field Service App.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"- **Daisuke**: @Servas, thank you. I need to see which of these fits within the software allowance without touching the frozen capital line.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"- **Sakura**: @Servas, I see them! But with the signal issues, D looks risky. Which one actually works without perfect conditions?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"- **Ryuji**: @Sakura, D is indeed risky. A directly targets the duplication I measured, which is the root of our daily losses.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Ryuji, A requires constant updates from every unit. With our staffing gap, who actually maintains that central catalog?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: @Asuka, a valid fear. My review shows tools needing daily entry from everyone were quietly dropped. A demands exactly that.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Servas, that confirms my worry. If A requires daily entry, it will likely be abandoned, leaving us with a broken tool and no budget to fix it.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"- **Sakura**: @Servas, that’s a huge red flag! If it needs everyone to type daily, it’s doomed. B sounds lighter, but does it need constant input too?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, B reads existing boards, so it doesn't demand new daily entry. It automates the summaries, reducing the manual burden rather than adding to it.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, B is passive, but it still generates output. Who reads and acts on those drafts? The two remaining clerks are already drowning in vendor queries.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: @Asuka, you are right. The narrow tools for one trade survived because they were simple. B is broad and complex, risking the same fate as the dropped daily-entry systems.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"- **Daisuke**: @Servas, I agree. B is too broad. C is just content, which might fit the software allowance, but does it solve the daily operational pain?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"- **Sakura**: @Daisuke, C is safe, but does it fix the broken records? I worry it’s just a band-aid on a bleeding wound.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, C addresses skill transfer, not the record duplication causing our daily losses. It solves a different problem entirely.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, C ignores the staffing crisis. We need a tool that reduces the manual load on the two remaining people, not one that adds more content to manage.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: @Asuka, you are right. C adds content, not capacity. We must choose the tool that actually lightens the daily burden.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"- **Daisuke**: @Servas, I agree. C is safe, but it doesn't fix the daily waste. I need to know if B fits the software allowance without capital costs.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Sakura,,"- **Sakura**: @Daisuke, B is software, so it fits! But if the signal drops, does it still work? I’m worried about the connection.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, B operates on internal task boards, not customer sites. The signal loss at plants doesn't affect internal workflow automation.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, that is true. But B still requires someone to review and circulate those drafts. With the coordination group empty, who takes that on?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
